description:
Design a 16-bit ones counter that takes a 16-bit input and outputs an 8-bit value representing the number of '1' bits in the input. The circuit iterates through each bit of the input data, incrementing a count whenever it encounters a '1', and then produces the final count as the output. This module is useful for applications requiring the analysis of bit density or signal characteristics in binary data.
module top_module(
    input [15:0] data_in,
    output reg [7:0] ones_out
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [15:0] data_in,
    output reg [7:0] ones_out
);integer i;
    reg [3:0] count;

    always @(*) begin
        count = 0;
        for (i = 0; i < 16; i = i + 1) begin
            if (data_in[i] == 1'b1) begin
                count = count + 1;
            end
        end
        ones_out = count;
    end

endmodule

