Design a reset synchronizer that ensures the output reset signal is stable and synchronized with the clock. The module takes an asynchronous reset input and utilizes a two-stage flip-flop configuration to eliminate potential metastability issues. The output, `rst_sync`, is the inverted value of the second flip-flop, providing a clean, synchronized reset signal that can be safely used in synchronous circuits.
