description:
Design a debouncer circuit that effectively filters noisy input signals from a push-button switch or similar sources. The circuit operates at a specified clock frequency and utilizes a configurable debounce time, measured in milliseconds. The debouncer counts clock cycles to determine whether the input signal has stabilized; when the input changes state, it resets the count and starts a duration timer based on the debounce time. Once the timer exceeds the specified debounce duration, the circuit updates the output to reflect the stable state of the input, ensuring that the output remains consistent and free from transient fluctuations.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input in,
  output reg out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input in,
  output reg out
);parameter clk_freq = 100000000;
parameter debounce_time = 50; // in milliseconds

reg [31:0] count;
reg [31:0] debounce_cycles;

always @(posedge clk) begin
  if (in != out) begin
    count <= 0;
    debounce_cycles <= debounce_time * clk_freq / 1000;
  end else if (count < debounce_cycles) begin
    count <= count + 1;
  end else begin
    out <= in;
  end
end

endmodule

