description:
Design a Johnson counter, a type of shift register that generates a specific sequence of states based on the feedback of its last output. This module has a parameterized output size (n), allowing it to dynamically create a counter with n flip-flops. On each rising edge of the clock input, the counter updates its state, with the output reflecting the current state. The next state is determined by the feedback mechanism, where the last output influences the subsequent states, thereby enabling a characteristic sequence of outputs that cycles through a defined pattern.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output [n-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  output [n-1:0] out
);parameter n = 4; // number of output signals

reg [n-1:0] state;
wire [n-1:0] next_state;

assign out = state;

always @ (posedge clk) begin
  state <= next_state;
end

assign next_state[0] = state[n-1];
generate
  genvar i;
  for (i = 1; i < n; i = i + 1) begin : loop
    assign next_state[i] = state[i-1] ^ state[n-1];
  end
endgenerate

endmodule

